Kernel
------

Fedora and Recovery build Linux stable v7.3.4, based on Torvalds Linux v7.3,
from kernel.org with local Liuqin adaptations. The kernel's COPYING, LICENSES
directory, file-level SPDX identifiers and original authorship are retained.
Exact sources are recorded in build/kernel/source.json and
build/recovery/kernel/source.json.

The Xiaomi kernel reference is MiCode/Xiaomi_Kernel_OpenSource, liuqin-t-oss
at eb49e10028e27fa98856cb5e458c0f0ec5b4554e. The patch headers identify
the relevant source files, functions and stock ROM components.

The Iris SM8450 platform layout references
pkgs/kernel/patches/0006-liuqin-media-iris.patch from Seeker0472/liuqin-nixos
commit 73e8071e09880aeb47f0a427b9a65b8cc10927c4.
The NanoSic Caps Lock management command draws on that revision's
pkgs/kernel/patches/0002-liuqin-input-hid-touchscreen.patch and
docs/PORTING-NOTES.md, adapted to the local connection and suspend lifecycle.
Folio posture support uses Seeker0472's GPIO23 active-low back-fold
measurements and host-side input suppression, with separate GPIO ownership,
MCU connector reports and explicit HID input releases.
https://github.com/Seeker0472/liuqin-nixos

For the panel, dtbo.img entry 15 defines the reset waveforms and the shared
M81 five-supply list with its post-switch waits (0112). The shipping msm_drm.ko
drives RESX low before releasing the supplies (0098). The same module checks
its clock request in dsi_display_prepare() (0102). Xiaomi's display clock
driver votes for voltage during clock prepare (0099). Choosing the first
DRM OPP is local to the Linux port.

For the M81 MDP and speaker I2C clocks (0110, 0111), the power supplies
come from the shipping Cape device tree. The operating levels follow
dispcc-waipio.c and gcc-waipio.c in Xiaomi's liuqin-t-oss kernel.

On Adreno, adreno_gen7_gmu.c clears and configures interrupts before GMU
start (0104). The Linux driver chooses its HFI interrupt mask for polled
firmware replies.

UFS lane clock ownership (0101) follows the symbol clocks in vendor_boot.img
and their management in ufs-qcom.c.

On the Bluetooth UART, Xiaomi stops RX and masks the main IRQ before
releasing resources. Linux serial-core system suspend needs an earlier
mask (0097). Xiaomi's hci_core.c queues HCI suspend preparation on the
request workqueue and bounds the wait (0105). The shipping QTI Bluetooth
HAL stops the IBS timers and tears down the handler, then creates a new
handler on UART initialization (0106).

The WCN6855 supply ranges (0107) come from the shipping device tree and
MiCode/kernel_devicetree at 1c507816ba8aa6117dcec41f577ef7a66d2091f7
(qcom/cape.dtsi). The RPMh, BT power and CNSS2 regulator drivers and the
Bluetooth HAL establish the startup votes and firmware handoff. See
docs/HARDWARE.md.

USB and charging
----------------

UCSI registration and connector-lifetime fixes in patch 0042 are adapted from
yzddmr6 and Codex's linux-sm8450-liuqin commits, respectively:
https://github.com/yzddmr6/linux-sm8450-liuqin/commit/9f9cd5ac3bc1fade2c2584a051913a2b03d506d2
https://github.com/yzddmr6/linux-sm8450-liuqin/commit/f43a4aa7fa89c6e227c5ec763e695576e66e2eb7
