The M81 charger classification (0100) uses the QC range in
qti_battery_charger_main_m81.ko and the USB enumeration in Xiaomi's
Android kernel for Linux power-supply reporting.

liuqin-mipps-auth (device/board-overlay/usr/local/libexec/liuqin-mipps-auth)
is derived from xiaomi-mipps-auth by ianchb and is licensed under
GPL-2.0-only. The file retains its SPDX identifier and authorship notice.
https://github.com/ianchb/xiaomi-mipps-auth

xiaoabiao contributed the liuqin adaptation and the standard PPS switch
(--allow-unverified-adapter). Role-first sequencing by yumo666666 and
current-attach verification are adapted from xiaomipad-6pro-mainline
commits 43aa1cb and 87f0250.
https://github.com/yzddmr6/xiaomipad-6pro-mainline/pull/7
https://github.com/yzddmr6/xiaomipad-6pro-mainline

For off-mode charging, the M81 vendor init rules in init.batterysecret.rc
and init.mi_thermald.rc start authentication and thermal control in charger
mode. The storage check and USB type log formatting use Linux interfaces.
docs/FASTCHARGE-SOURCES.md records the init file hashes and log ABI.

FastRPC and sensors
-------------------

Pinned repositories and revisions: device/sensors/sources.manifest.

* hexagonrpc: https://github.com/linux-msm/hexagonrpc
  GPL-3.0-or-later; see its COPYING and source file notices.
* libssc: https://codeberg.org/DylanVanAssche/libssc
  GPL-3.0-or-later; see its LICENSE and source file notices.
* iio-sensor-proxy: https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/hadess/iio-sensor-proxy
  GPL-3.0-or-later; see its COPYING and source file notices.

The patches under device/sensors/patches retain the licenses of the components
they modify.

In the kernel, Xiaomi's adsprpc.c recovers an interrupted DSP invocation.
The Linux FastRPC driver uses a freezer-aware wait to preserve a userspace
invocation across system sleep (0103).

The hexagonrpc listener uses the continuation protocol in Qualcomm fastrpc
3b7f929145db1a52a8d0a334805defefd287e97e (src/listener_android.c and
inc/adsp_listener.h). The Linux port also checks that both calls report
the same total length.

Audio
-----

The AudioReach board topology source and build script carry BSD-3-Clause
identifiers. Xiaomi-Pad-6-Pro-tplg.bin is generated from the topology
source. It is not classified as proprietary DSP firmware.

The M81 capture sequence (0108) follows /vendor/lib64/libagm_pcm_plugin.so
and /vendor/lib64/libagm.so. The LPASS hardware votes (0109) are named in
the vendor_boot device tree. Their order comes from lpass_cdc_dlkm.ko.
docs/AUDIO.md identifies the Qualcomm driver sources for these votes.

Fingerprint integration
-----------------------

Optional device/fingerprint/oem source retains file-level BSD-2-Clause,
LGPL-2.1-or-later, GPL-2.0-or-later and Apache-2.0 notices. QSEE supplicant/QCBOR
retain upstream BSD licenses. QSEE supplicant is by Dawid Wróbel
(https://github.com/wrobelda/qsee-supplicant); QCBOR is by Laurence Lundblade
(https://github.com/laurencelundblade/QCBOR). Exact dependencies are in
